NAME
    writers - find static write references to an address

SYNOPSIS
    writers <addr> [<scanstart> <scanlen>]

DESCRIPTION
    Scans CpuBus for instructions that statically store to hex address
    <addr>. By default the scan covers <addr>'s own bank from $8000 to
    $FFFF; supply hex <scanstart> and <scanlen> to scan another range.

    Only statically encoded addressing modes (absolute and absolute-long)
    are detected. Indexed or indirect writes are not visible to static
    analysis; use watch(1) or 'bp write' in bp(1) for runtime write
    detection.

EXAMPLES
    writers 13c6
    writers 13c6 808000 8000

EXIT STATUS
    0   Scan completed (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, invalid hex argument, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    readers(1), callers(1), watch(1), bp(1), disasm(1)
